stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: Zendesk intake - all six persisted intent states
  accDescr: Creation persists an attempt before POST. Creating or uncertain work can only recover by observation and linking, never by an automatic second create request.
  direction TB
  state "prepared" as Prepared
  state "creating" as Creating
  state "uncertain" as Uncertain
  state "linked" as Linked
  state "blocked" as Blocked
  state "withdrawn" as Withdrawn

  [*] --> Prepared: eligible tagged report
  Prepared --> Prepared: preflight unavailable
  Prepared --> Withdrawn: eligibility withdrawn
  Withdrawn --> Prepared: eligible again / unattempted
  Prepared --> Creating: audit snapshot and attempt
  Prepared --> Linked: marked issue / matching mapping
  Prepared --> Blocked: identity collision
  Creating --> Linked: ID observed and linked
  Creating --> Uncertain: unconfirmed outcome
  Creating --> Blocked: mapping conflict
  Uncertain --> Uncertain: not uniquely observed
  Uncertain --> Linked: unique recovery
  Uncertain --> Blocked: mapping conflict
  Blocked --> Linked: matching mapping observed

  note right of Creating
    Key: every named state is persisted.
    Audit precedes POST; recovery never blindly repeats it.
  end note
  note right of Linked
    Intake complete; field reconciliation continues.
    Linking is not state approval.
  end note
